      "problem": "Find the solutions of the equation $25{p}^{2}+9=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{p}^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ 25{p}^{2} & =-9 \\\\ {p}^{2} & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\np=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{25}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
